{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#984","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#984","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#984\",\"parent_revision\":\"4b87e9984459d2bf368554abd37c77e6f48fc7c418e38883208bf92b4688f06c\",\"root_revision\":\"4b87e9984459d2bf368554abd37c77e6f48fc7c418e38883208bf92b4688f06c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe artifact manifest system (P965) stores manifests in GitHub Issue body with HTML comment delimiters. This works but has limitations: body edits can corrupt delimiters, and the same approach won't work for Linear (which uses Attachments) or GitLab. Research completed on GitHub Issue Fields (public preview 2026-03-12), GitHub Projects V2 fields, pinned comments, Linear attachments API, and GitLab (pending). The ArtifactBackend Protocol abstraction exists but only has one provider (GitHubArtifactProvider). Success: multiple providers exist, each using the backend's native storage primitive. Research files: /tmp/research-github-projects-v2-fields.md, /tmp/research-linear-custom-fields.md, /tmp/research-gitlab-custom-fields.md (pending).\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Backend-first artifact storage providers\\nDate: 2026-04-05\\nGoal: Add multiple concrete ArtifactBackend providers (GitHub Gists, Linear Attachments, GitLab Snippets) so artifact manifests use each platform's native storage primitive instead of HTML comment delimiters.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. ArtifactBackend Protocol interface defined (backlog_core/artifact_provider.py:170) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Grep class ArtifactBackend(Protocol)\\n2. TestArtifactBackendProtocol behavioral contract test suite exists (tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py:130) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Grep class TestArtifactBackendProtocol\\n3. Existing GitHubArtifactProvider available as reference implementation | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Grep class GitHubArtifactProvider:288\\n4. GitHub storage primitive API specification | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User decision \u2014 GitHub Gists API (stable, not public-preview Issue Fields)\\n5. Linear storage primitive API specification | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker VERIFIED Linear Attachments API via research/artifact-manifest-linear-patterns.md\\n6. GitLab storage primitive | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User decision \u2014 GitLab Snippets API (POST /projects/:id/snippets), direct equivalent of GitHub Gists; custom fields REFUTED as unsuitable\\n7. BacklogBackend injection points (server.py \u00d7 6 sites, operations.py, sam_schema/server.py) | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst, 17-file Impact Radius\\n8. Auth credential injection pattern | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst \u2014 runtime config via env var in server.py\\n9. ArtifactBackend instantiation scope | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst \u2014 _get_artifact_provider() at server.py:2117\\n10. Impact radius \u2014 all callers identified | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst \u2014 17 files across 6 categories\\n\\nNew conditions discovered by swarm:\\n11. Migration script scope (dh_migrate.py, migrate_plan_artifacts.py) | Snapshot: N/A \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User decision \u2014 scripts are GitHub-only migrations by design; excluded from #984\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 4: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (user redirected from Issue Fields public-preview to Gists API)\\n- Condition 5: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (fact-checker confirmed Linear Attachments API)\\n- Condition 6: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (was BLOCKED on GitLab custom fields refuted; user resolved via GitLab Snippets)\\n- Conditions 7\u201310: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (impact-analyst mapped all injection points)\\n- Condition 11: (new) AVAILABLE (migration scripts explicitly excluded from scope by user)\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 11\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **backend-first artifact storage providers** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 discovered during #965 implementation session 2026-03-21\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-05)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**P2 \u2014 Valuable but not blocking**\\n\\nThis work completes the provider abstraction started in P965, but it only affects users running Linear or GitLab backends. Those backends have no production users yet \u2014 the GitHub backend is the only production path. P0 and P1 items address active production failures and regressions. #984 delivers correctness and portability improvements for future multi-backend deployments. Scheduling as P2 ensures it gets done before the backends ship to real users, without displacing in-flight critical work.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n**Developer-facing only \u2014 no CLI or user-facing surface changes.**\\n\\nAffected parties:\\n- Backend contributors adding Linear or GitLab support: currently blocked by missing provider implementations; after this work, `ArtifactBackend` is fully implemented for all three backends\\n- Test authors: `TestArtifactBackendProtocol` parameterization ensures new providers are tested to the same standard as GitHub\\n- Future backend integrators: the provider factory pattern makes adding a fourth backend a single-class addition\\n\\nNo changes to CLI commands, MCP tool signatures, or user-visible output. The artifact storage mechanism is an internal implementation detail.\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\n**In scope:**\\n- Implement `LinearArtifactProvider` class in `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` using the Linear Attachments API\\n- Implement `GitLabArtifactProvider` class in `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` using the GitLab Snippets API (`POST /projects/:id/snippets`)\\n- Update or supplement `GitHubArtifactProvider` to use the GitHub Gists API (replacing HTML comment delimiters)\\n- Implement `_get_artifact_provider()` factory in `backlog_core/server.py` and `sam_schema/server.py` that selects the correct provider based on runtime backend config\\n- Update all hardcoded `GitHubArtifactProvider` type annotations in `server.py` to `ArtifactBackend`\\n- Parameterize `TestArtifactBackendProtocol` to run against all three concrete providers\\n- Update `docs/backend-providers.md` to reflect the multi-provider implementation\\n\\n**Out of scope:**\\n- Migration scripts (`dh_migrate.py`, `migrate_plan_artifacts.py`) \u2014 GitHub-only by design; these scripts operate on GitHub Issues specifically and are not part of the general provider abstraction\\n- GitLab Issue Fields API or Linear custom fields \u2014 research confirmed these are unsuitable; Snippets/Attachments APIs are the correct approach\\n- User-facing CLI surface changes \u2014 this is an internal wiring change only\\n- New backend types beyond GitHub, Linear, and GitLab\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n1. **Portability**: Users on Linear or GitLab backends gain the same artifact persistence that GitHub users already have. Artifacts (implementation plans, verification reports, research files) are stored in the native platform rather than being silently dropped.\\n2. **Reliability**: GitHub Gists API is a stable, dedicated storage API. The current HTML comment delimiter approach is fragile \u2014 delimiter corruption has been a known failure mode. Switching to Gists eliminates this class of bugs.\\n3. **Protocol correctness**: All three providers implement the full `ArtifactBackend` Protocol from P965. Type checker enforcement (ty) catches missing methods at development time rather than at runtime.\\n4. **Test coverage parity**: Parameterized tests ensure no provider silently regresses. A bug in any one provider shows up in the same test suite that already covers the others.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen implementation is complete:\\n\\n- `backlog_core/server.py` contains `_get_artifact_provider()` factory that reads the runtime backend config and returns the appropriate `ArtifactBackend` instance: `GitHubArtifactProvider` for GitHub, `LinearArtifactProvider` for Linear, `GitLabArtifactProvider` for GitLab\\n- `sam_schema/server.py` uses the same factory pattern (not a direct `GitHubArtifactProvider` instantiation)\\n- All 6 hardcoded `GitHubArtifactProvider` type annotations in `server.py` (lines 2100, 2117, 2134, 2711, 3367, 3454) are updated to `ArtifactBackend`\\n- `TestArtifactBackendProtocol` in `tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py` runs against all three concrete providers via pytest parameterization\\n- `test_backlog_update_artifact_registration.py` patches the correct import path after any `operations.py` changes\\n- `docs/backend-providers.md` documents all three providers with their respective API details\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `LinearArtifactProvider` class exists in `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` and implements all methods of the `ArtifactBackend` Protocol using the Linear Attachments API\\n2. `GitLabArtifactProvider` class exists in `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` and implements all methods of the `ArtifactBackend` Protocol using the GitLab Snippets API (`POST /projects/:id/snippets`)\\n3. `GitHubArtifactProvider` updated to use GitHub Gists API \u2014 HTML comment delimiter storage is replaced or no longer the primary path\\n4. `_get_artifact_provider()` factory exists in `backlog_core/server.py` and returns the correct provider instance based on the runtime backend config (GitHub \u2192 `GitHubArtifactProvider`, Linear \u2192 `LinearArtifactProvider`, GitLab \u2192 `GitLabArtifactProvider`)\\n5. All 6 hardcoded `GitHubArtifactProvider` type annotations in `backlog_core/server.py` updated to `ArtifactBackend`\\n6. `TestArtifactBackendProtocol` in `tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py` is parameterized to run against all three concrete providers\\n7. `test_backlog_update_artifact_registration.py` patches updated to reflect any import path changes in `operations.py`\\n8. `sam_schema/server.py` updated to use provider factory \u2014 no direct `GitHubArtifactProvider` instantiation\\n9. `docs/backend-providers.md` updated to document all three providers, their APIs, and configuration\\n10. All existing tests pass; new provider tests achieve coverage parity with existing GitHub provider tests\\n11. Migration scripts (`dh_migrate.py`, `migrate_plan_artifacts.py`) are UNCHANGED \u2014 they are GitHub-only by design\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n- **Research artifacts on issue #984** (6 files registered):\\n  - `research/task-management/artifact-manifest-backend-providers.md` \u2014 implementation sketches for `LinearArtifactProvider` (line 100) and `GitLabArtifactProvider` (line 124); primary implementation reference\\n  - `research/artifact-manifest-linear-patterns.md` \u2014 Linear Attachments API confirmed as correct storage mechanism\\n  - Additional research files registered against the issue (fetch via `artifact_list(selector='#984')`)\\n- **GitHub Gists API**: https://docs.github.com/en/rest/gists \u2014 stable REST API for creating/reading/updating gists; use as `GitHubArtifactProvider` storage backend\\n- **Linear Attachments API**: documented in `research/artifact-manifest-linear-patterns.md`; confirmed by fact-checker\\n- **GitLab Snippets API**: https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/api/project_snippets.html \u2014 `POST /projects/:id/snippets` is the direct GitLab equivalent of GitHub Gists\\n- **`ArtifactBackend` Protocol**: `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py:170` \u2014 Protocol definition; `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py:288` \u2014 existing `GitHubArtifactProvider` reference implementation\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n| File | Change Type | Notes |\\n|------|------------|-------|\\n| `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` | CODE CHANGE | Add `LinearArtifactProvider`, `GitLabArtifactProvider`; update `GitHubArtifactProvider` to Gists API; reference at lines 170, 288 |\\n| `backlog_core/server.py` | CODE CHANGE + TYPE CHANGE | Add `_get_artifact_provider()` factory; update 6 `GitHubArtifactProvider` type annotations (lines 2100, 2117, 2134, 2711, 3367, 3454) to `ArtifactBackend` |\\n| `backlog_core/operations.py` | CODE CHANGE | Update import and instantiation at lines 26, 761 to use factory |\\n| `sam_schema/server.py` | CODE CHANGE | Update provider wiring at lines 28, 387 to use factory instead of direct instantiation |\\n| `tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py` | TEST UPDATE | Parameterize `TestArtifactBackendProtocol` at line 130 to cover all 3 providers |\\n| `tests_backlog/test_backlog_update_artifact_registration.py` | TEST UPDATE | Update 6 patch locations if `operations.py` import path changes |\\n| `docs/backend-providers.md` | DOC UPDATE | Update stale sections to reflect multi-provider implementation |\\n| `backlog_core/__init__.py` | CODE CHANGE | Export new provider classes if currently exported |\\n| `backlog_core/types.py` | CODE CHANGE | Type definitions if any provider-specific types needed |\\n| `tests_backlog/test_linear_artifact_provider.py` | NEW CODE | New test file for `LinearArtifactProvider` (coverage parity) |\\n| `tests_backlog/test_gitlab_artifact_provider.py` | NEW CODE | New test file for `GitLabArtifactProvider` (coverage parity) |\\n| `tests_backlog/conftest.py` | CODE CHANGE | Add fixtures for Linear/GitLab provider test setup |\\n| `backlog_core/backends/linear.py` | CODE CHANGE | Linear client API integration if Attachments API call is here |\\n| `backlog_core/backends/gitlab.py` | CODE CHANGE | GitLab client API integration if Snippets API call is here |\\n| `dh_migrate.py` | UNCHANGED | GitHub-only by design; excluded from scope |\\n| `migrate_plan_artifacts.py` | UNCHANGED | GitHub-only by design; excluded from scope |\\n| `research/task-management/artifact-manifest-backend-providers.md` | UNCHANGED | Reference artifact; consumed but not modified |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- **P965** (artifact manifest system) \u2014 COMPLETED. Provides the `ArtifactBackend` Protocol definition and `GitHubArtifactProvider` reference implementation that #984 extends. The Protocol interface is the contract all three providers must satisfy.\\n- **P389** (pluggable `BacklogBackend`) \u2014 COMPLETED. Provides the `BacklogBackend` Protocol and backend selection mechanism that #984's provider factory mirrors. The factory pattern for `_get_artifact_provider()` follows the same architecture established by P389.\\n\\nNo blocking open dependencies. Both foundations are merged and available.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Medium complexity \u2014 high confidence estimate**\\n\\nWork breakdown:\\n- 3 new provider classes: `LinearArtifactProvider`, `GitLabArtifactProvider`, and `GitHubArtifactProvider` Gists update\\n- 1 factory function (`_get_artifact_provider()`) wired into 2 servers (`backlog_core/server.py`, `sam_schema/server.py`)\\n- Type annotation updates at 6 known locations in `server.py`\\n- Test parameterization of `TestArtifactBackendProtocol` + 2 new provider test files\\n- Documentation update for `docs/backend-providers.md`\\n\\n**Why high confidence**: The `ArtifactBackend` Protocol is fully defined (P965). The `GitHubArtifactProvider` is a complete reference implementation to copy structure from. Research artifacts contain implementation sketches for both Linear and GitLab providers (lines 100, 124 of `artifact-manifest-backend-providers.md`).\\n\\n**Risk factor**: GitLab Snippets API has no prior implementation in this codebase \u2014 some API research overhead expected. Mitigated by available research artifacts and official API documentation. The GitLab backend is structurally simpler than Linear (REST vs GraphQL).\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| research | research/artifact-manifest-linear-patterns.md | current | artifact-migrate | 2026-03-22T05:59:41.536590+00:00 |\\n| research | research/artifact-manifest-jira-asana-monday-patterns.md | current | artifact-migrate | 2026-03-22T05:59:44.902521+00:00 |\\n| research | research/artifact-manifest-github-fields.md | current | artifact-migrate | 2026-03-22T05:59:48.525429+00:00 |\\n| research | research/artifact-manifest-linear-custom-fields.md | current | artifact-migrate | 2026-03-22T05:59:52.207421+00:00 |\\n| research | research/artifact-manifest-gitlab-custom-fields.md | current | artifact-migrate | 2026-03-22T05:59:55.892611+00:00 |\\n| research | research/artifact-manifest-gitlab-api-deep.md | current | artifact-migrate | 2026-03-22T05:59:59.488305+00:00 |\\n| feature-context | plan/feature-context-backend-first-artifact-storage-providers.md | current | discovery | 2026-04-05T03:52:05.281177+00:00 |\\n| architect | plan/architect-backend-first-artifact-storage-providers.md | current | python-cli-design-spec | 2026-04-05T04:17:17.142513+00:00 |\\n| task-plan | /home/ubuntulinuxqa2/.dh/projects/-home-ubuntulinuxqa2-repos-claude_skills/plan/P984-backend-first-artifact-storage-providers.yaml | current | sam_create | 2026-04-05T04:27:19Z |\\n| task-plan | plan/P984-backend-first-artifact-storage-providers.yaml | current |  | 2026-04-05T04:28:26Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fact Check Summary Backend First Artifact Storage Providers\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim 1: VERIFIED**\\n- Claim: \\\"ArtifactBackend Protocol abstraction exists but only has one provider (GitHubArtifactProvider)\\\"\\n- Evidence: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py:170` defines `class ArtifactBackend(Protocol)` and line 288 defines `class GitHubArtifactProvider`\\n- Source: Direct code inspection via Grep\\n\\n**Claim 2: VERIFIED**\\n- Claim: \\\"GitHub Issue Fields public preview API was announced 2026-03-12\\\"\\n- Evidence: GitHub Blog Changelog entry at `https://github.blog/changelog/2026-03-12-issue-fields-structured-issue-metadata-is-in-public-preview/`\\n- Source: `research/artifact-manifest-github-fields.md` (line 69, 229)\\n\\n**Claim 3: VERIFIED**\\n- Claim: \\\"Linear uses an Attachments API for structured metadata\\\"\\n- Evidence: Linear's GraphQL API exposes Attachments with webhook support for attachment change events; Linear Developer docs confirm \\\"Issue attachments\\\" are a first-class webhook event type\\n- Source: `research/artifact-manifest-linear-patterns.md` (lines 207-210, 230)\\n\\n**Claim 4: REFUTED**\\n- Claim: \\\"GitLab has a native metadata storage primitive suitable for artifact manifests\\\"\\n- Actual finding: GitLab has custom fields (text, number, single/multi-select) but they are NOT suitable for artifact manifests:\\n  - Text field max 1,024 characters (too small for manifests)\\n  - No REST API for custom fields (only UI)\\n  - GraphQL write mutations NOT documented or working (users report schema errors)\\n  - Cannot store structured JSON/nested data\\n  - Max 50 fields per group, 10 per work item type\\n- Sources: `research/artifact-manifest-gitlab-custom-fields.md` (lines 27, 36, 80-81) and `research/artifact-manifest-gitlab-api-deep.md` (lines 121-137, 185-186, 204)\\n\\n**Claim 5: VERIFIED**\\n- Claim: \\\"Tests \u2014 TestArtifactBackendProtocol \u2014 exist as a behavioral contract test suite\\\"\\n- Evidence: `plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py:130` defines `class TestArtifactBackendProtocol`\\n- Source: Direct code inspection via Grep\\n\\n**Claim 6: VERIFIED**\\n- Claim: \\\"The HTML comment delimiter approach (<!-- artifact-manifest:begin --> ... end) is the current storage mechanism\\\"\\n- Evidence: String delimiters `artifact-manifest:begin` and `artifact-manifest:end` found in 3 files:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py`\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_registry.py`\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py`\\n- Source: Grep pattern search\\n</div>\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **5 VERIFIED** \u2014 Claims 1, 2, 3, 5, 6 are accurate per primary sources\\n- **1 REFUTED** \u2014 Claim 4 overstates GitLab's capability; custom fields exist but are unsuitable for artifact manifest storage due to character limits, missing API, and inability to store structured data\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius Backend First Artifact Storage Providers\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Scope**: Adding `LinearArtifactProvider` and `GitLabArtifactProvider` to `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` alongside the existing `GitHubArtifactProvider`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Code Producers** (files that implement ArtifactBackend):\\n\\n- `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py:170` \u2014 `ArtifactBackend` Protocol definition \u2014 no Protocol change needed; new providers added here\\n- `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py:288` \u2014 `GitHubArtifactProvider` \u2014 reference implementation; no change; serves as template for new providers\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Code Consumers** (files that call ArtifactBackend methods or instantiate providers):\\n\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:2100` \u2014 `_artifact_provider: GitHubArtifactProvider | None` singleton type annotation \u2014 **BREAKS**: hardcoded to concrete class; must become `ArtifactBackend | None`\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:2117` \u2014 `_get_artifact_provider() -> GitHubArtifactProvider` return type \u2014 **BREAKS**: must become `-> ArtifactBackend`; factory logic needs provider-selection by backend config\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:2134` \u2014 instantiates `GitHubArtifactProvider(...)` in factory \u2014 **CODE CHANGE**: needs provider selection (GitHub / Linear / GitLab) based on runtime config\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:2711` \u2014 second direct instantiation `GitHubArtifactProvider(...)` \u2014 **CODE CHANGE**: same provider selection logic\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:3367` \u2014 helper function param `provider: GitHubArtifactProvider` \u2014 **BREAKS**: type annotation; must be `ArtifactBackend`\\n- `backlog_core/server.py:3454` \u2014 helper function param `provider: GitHubArtifactProvider` \u2014 **BREAKS**: type annotation; must be `ArtifactBackend`\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py:26,761` \u2014 imports and instantiates `GitHubArtifactProvider(repo=resolve_repo(repo))` \u2014 **CODE CHANGE**: needs provider selection logic; import must change if factory is centralised\\n- `sam_schema/server.py:28,387` \u2014 independent server that imports and instantiates `GitHubArtifactProvider` directly \u2014 **CODE CHANGE**: second server, easy to miss; needs same provider selection treatment\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Code Other References** (import or reference without direct calls):\\n\\n- `backlog_core/artifact_registry.py:209` \u2014 docstring cross-reference to `ArtifactBackend` \u2014 **STALE**: minor doc update when new providers land\\n- `backlog_core/backend_protocol.py:8-9` \u2014 comment cites `ArtifactBackend` as the established pattern for async wrapping \u2014 no change needed\\n- `scripts/migrate_plan_artifacts.py:39,345,446,514-516` \u2014 imports and instantiates `GitHubArtifactProvider` directly (migration script) \u2014 **QUESTION**: appears GitHub-only by design; clarification needed on whether migration scripts should become provider-agnostic\\n- `scripts/dh_migrate.py:48,908,983,992` \u2014 same pattern as migrate_plan_artifacts.py \u2014 **QUESTION**: same provider-agnostic question\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Documentation** (files that describe current behavior):\\n\\n- `docs/backend-providers.md:97,214,282,291,294,357,623-626` \u2014 describes `ArtifactBackend` Protocol and `GitHubArtifactProvider` as the current single implementation; table at line 214 lists #984 as \\\"groomed\\\" \u2014 **STALE**: multiple sections need update: implementation table, design principles section, DocumentBackend Protocol section. Also lists `GitHubArtifactProvider` as sole example throughout.\\n- `research/task-management/artifact-manifest-backend-providers.md` \u2014 comparative analysis of GitHub/Linear/GitLab/Supabase for `ArtifactBackend`; contains implementation sketches for `LinearArtifactProvider` (line 100) and `GitLabArtifactProvider` (line 124) \u2014 **becomes implementation reference** for this feature; no content update needed\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Configuration / CI** (CI workflows, config files):\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` and others \u2014 no explicit test_artifact or artifact_provider filtering; artifact tests run as part of the full pytest suite \u2014 **no CI gap**: new provider tests automatically included in existing matrix\\n- No workflow-level artifact provider configuration \u2014 provider selection is runtime config (repo env var in server.py), not build-time\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Agent Instructions** (skills, agents that instruct artifact storage use):\\n\\n- No skill or agent files in `plugins/development-harness/skills/` reference `ArtifactBackend`, `artifact_provider`, or `GitHubArtifactProvider` \u2014 **0 files found**: no agent/skill changes required\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Tests** (files covering ArtifactBackend):\\n\\n- `tests_backlog/test_artifact_provider.py:130` \u2014 `TestArtifactBackendProtocol` \u2014 currently only validates `GitHubArtifactProvider` against Protocol \u2014 **CONTENT UPDATE**: should be parameterized to run all three providers; `_InMemoryArtifactBackend` at line 485 already satisfies Protocol correctly\\n- `tests_backlog/test_backlog_update_artifact_registration.py:47,83,99,114,126,148` \u2014 patches `backlog_core.operations.GitHubArtifactProvider` \u2014 **BREAKS** if `operations.py` changes its import (e.g., to use a factory or base import from `artifact_provider`)\\n- `tests/test_artifact_content_storage.py:28-65` \u2014 tests GitHub-specific methods, patches `_get_artifact_provider` via `backlog_core.server` \u2014 **unaffected**: patches the server function, not the concrete class; GitHub-specific method tests remain valid\\n- `tests/test_dh_paths_integration.py:440-560` \u2014 instantiates `GitHubArtifactProvider` for path traversal / root isolation tests \u2014 **STALE**: new providers with different path semantics (Linear stores remotely; GitLab may store differently) need provider-specific path tests or skip markers\\n- `tests/test_backlog_core_paths.py:207` \u2014 `TestGitHubArtifactProviderRootWorktree` \u2014 GitHub-specific constructor test \u2014 **unchanged**\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Systems Inventory**: 17 files across 6 categories\\n\\n**Ecosystem Completeness Checklist**:\\n- [x] All Protocol implementors found (artifact_provider.py \u2014 1 existing, 2 to add)\\n- [x] All callers found (server.py \u00d7 6 sites, operations.py, sam_schema/server.py)\\n- [x] All docs found (backend-providers.md, research entry)\\n- [x] All tests found (test_artifact_provider.py, test_artifact_content_storage.py, test_dh_paths_integration.py, test_backlog_core_paths.py, test_backlog_update_artifact_registration.py)\\n- [x] CI coverage verified (no explicit filtering; full pytest suite covers artifact tests)\\n\\n**Risk flags**:\\n1. `server.py` has 4 hardcoded `GitHubArtifactProvider` type annotations \u2014 ty will error without coordinated type changes\\n2. `test_backlog_update_artifact_registration.py` patches the concrete import path \u2014 fragile if operations.py import changes\\n3. `sam_schema/server.py` is a second independent server \u2014 easy to miss in implementation\\n4. Migration scripts (dh_migrate.py, migrate_plan_artifacts.py) are GitHub-only by design \u2014 scope decision needed before planning\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a3b427d76410564e28c7bde5bf2e93f907bb9a90aaa3c1e4923d89f5ea22b7e6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVWC53A\"}"}